  <h2>Why test for radon</h2>
  <p>Radon is a colorless, odorless radioactive gas produced by the natural breakdown of uranium in soil and rock. It can enter buildings through the foundation. Testing is the only way to know a building's radon level, and the U.S. EPA recommends testing homes for radon.</p>

  <h2>Who it's for</h2>
  <p>Homeowners, and builders and design teams who need a radon test for a project.</p>

